act Us&lt;/h1&gt;\n        &lt;form action="{{ url_for(\'contact_us\') }}" method="post"&gt;\n            &lt;label for="contact-name-input"&gt;Name:&lt;/label&gt;\n            &lt;input type="text" id="contact-name-input" name="contact_name" required&gt;\n            &lt;label for="contact-email-input"&gt;Email:&lt;/label&gt;\n            &lt;input type="email" id="contact-email-input" name="contact_email" required&gt;\n            &lt;label for="contact-message-area"&gt;Message:&lt;/label&gt;\n            &lt;textarea id="contact-message-area" name="contact_message" required&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;\n            &lt;button type="submit" id="send-message-button"&gt;Send Message&lt;/button&gt;\n        &lt;/form&gt;\n        {% with messages = get_flashed_messages(with_categories=true) %}\n            {% if messages %}\n                &lt;ul&gt;\n                {% for category, message in messages %}\n                    &lt;li class="{{ category }}"&gt;{{ message }}&lt;/li&gt;\n                {% endfor %}\n                &lt;/ul&gt;\n            {% endif %}\n        {% endwith %}\n        &lt;div id="confirmation-message"&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;!-- Section for displaying flashed messages --&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n\n\n', 'images': '', 'comments': 'After reviewing the provided code and the regulations set forth by ChatDev, I have identified several areas that require attention. Below is a detailed assessment based on the regulations, followed by the highest priority comment and suggested revisions.\n\n### Review of Regulations\n\n1. Accessing the website at http://localhost:5000: \n   - This is correctly set up in the app.run(port=5000) line in app.py.\n\n2. Checking if the \'/\' route exists: \n   - The route for the login page (\'/\') is correctly defined in the login() function.\n\n3. Using routing in frontend code: \n   - The frontend code correctly uses url_for() to generate URLs for routing instead of hardcoding HTML file names.\n\n4.